From 4da3c6b349e4db5aa92a4ac8290d12083f8901f0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kernel <kernel@local>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 03:26:38 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 8/8] ik2: IK2_K_WEXP skips Q8_0 (its register kernel's sums
 were not row_dot_2's bits on gfx1100)

- experts_win_q8_gu/_down_kernel removed; experts_win_gu/_down return false for Q8_0, so a window's
  Q8_0 experts stay on experts_*_mem (the token path's bits)
- q8_blk0_dot / q8_blk1_dot back to the v1.1.75 text (the word-taking split could move HIP's FMA fusion
  in the token kernels too)
- cause: HIP's default contraction (fast-honor-pragmas, AMDGPU aggressive FMA fusion) fuses the Q8_0
  pair's long sums per SelectionDAG basic block; the register kernel's DAG (words from another block,
  gate then up) fused differently from row_dot_2's loads-beside-sums
- tests: Q8_0 checks 'not taken'; same_bits() prints the count and first differing value of each
  failing window check
---
 docs/INKLING2.md          |   9 +-
 src/ik2/ik2_kernels.cu    | 171 +++++++-------------------------------
 src/ik2/ik2_kernels.cuh   |   6 +-
 tests/ik2_kernels_test.cu |  82 ++++++++++++++----
 4 files changed, 105 insertions(+), 163 deletions(-)

diff --git a/docs/INKLING2.md b/docs/INKLING2.md
index ef2d9ad4..b72da5fa 100644
--- a/docs/INKLING2.md
+++ b/docs/INKLING2.md
@@ -486,10 +486,11 @@ VRAM; lane parity (`IK2_LANE=1`) sums in other bits there and is a test option.
 
 **The exact window's register kernels** (each off unless set to 1; on, every token's values the same bits - held by
 `ik2_kernels_test`'s `test_window_k`): `IK2_K_WEXP` a window's experts with a row's words read once into the
-registers for all of its group's tokens (NVFP4, Q8_0, Q4_K gate / up; NVFP4, Q8_0, Q5_0 down; non-temporal where the
-token kernels are, `IK2_HIP_NT`), where `experts_*_mem` read a group's rows from the caches once a member and wait on
-each step's loads; `IK2_K_WMVF16` the window's FP16 rows (router, dynamic taps, sinks) with their loads asked for
-first; `IK2_K_WROUTE` the router's rows, the picks and their groups in one launch (two less a visit);
+registers for all of its group's tokens (NVFP4, Q4_K gate / up; NVFP4, Q5_0 down; non-temporal where the token kernels
+are, `IK2_HIP_NT`; Q8_0 stays on `experts_*_mem`: a register kernel over its sums gave other bits on gfx1100, the
+compiler fusing its long sums into FMAs differently), where `experts_*_mem` read a group's rows from the caches once a
+member and wait on each step's loads; `IK2_K_WMVF16` the window's FP16 rows (router, dynamic taps, sinks) with their
+loads asked for first; `IK2_K_WROUTE` the router's rows, the picks and their groups in one launch (two less a visit);
 `IK2_K_WCOMB` the MoE's combine and its conv in one launch (one less a visit); `IK2_K_WACOMB` the tokens' attention
 combine with its partials asked for 32 at a time (`IK2_HIP_COMB`'s combine).
 
